2026-09-02 11:48:25,462 [INFO] We chose Cosine Similarity because it measures the angle between two vectors in high-dimensional space, focusing purely on the 'direction' of the meaning rather than the 'magnitude' (which can be skewed by the length of the original text or word frequencies). A score closer to 1 means the vectors point in the same semantic direction (highly similar), while a score near 0 means they are orthogonal (unrelated). This is the standard and most robust metric for comparing text embeddings.
